WEBVTT

00:00:15.010 --> 00:00:22.080
Looking up at the purple panorama of the galaxy highway...

00:00:24.050 --> 00:00:30.190
...a shooting star pierces my heart.

00:00:30.360 --> 00:00:38.000
synchronized with the sleepless city...
My accelerating heartbeat is

00:00:39.280 --> 00:00:44.770
...and I suddenly pray for the unseen tomorrow...

00:00:45.640 --> 00:00:50.010
...that brings that melody.

00:00:51.810 --> 00:00:56.950
A mysterious voice won't let me go.

00:00:57.490 --> 00:01:03.560
Oh, tell me seventh moon, this frustrated heart...

00:01:04.560 --> 00:01:09.330
...where will you take me to?

00:01:09.770 --> 00:01:15.840
To sway in the blue seventh moon...

00:01:16.270 --> 00:01:25.750
...searching for the answer to the rhythm in this crazy dance.

00:01:32.590 --> 00:01:37.870
He's Unified Forces ace pilot
Lt Gamlin Kizaki of Diamond Force.

00:01:37.870 --> 00:01:40.790
Mylene, I want to arrange
things between you and Gamlin.

00:01:43.400 --> 00:01:44.350
Arrange things ?!

00:01:44.900 --> 00:01:47.050
What's your connection
with the military ?!

00:01:49.100 --> 00:01:53.200
The VF-19 has the latest
weapons installed ! Attack !

00:02:04.500 --> 00:02:06.240
You made me shoot !

00:02:20.200 --> 00:02:26.140
Summer Accident

00:02:26.500 --> 00:02:32.840
And for dinner, we have a
complete assortment of seafood.

00:02:33.950 --> 00:02:39.920
We have all kinds of water entertainment
activities on the marine resort ship Riviera.

00:02:39.920 --> 00:02:47.080
Swimming, yachting, surfing,
jet skiing, and trolling.

00:02:47.080 --> 00:02:52.300
Of course, the waves are artificial, but
this is a versatile, high class resort ship.

00:02:52.950 --> 00:02:56.800
The temperature is set at
a pleasant summer climate.

00:02:58.560 --> 00:03:01.750
This wide ocean is used
not only for leisure...

00:03:01.750 --> 00:03:07.860
...but also for research, marine farming,
and the fish are also used as food.

00:03:08.430 --> 00:03:11.900
And for dinner, we have...

00:03:11.900 --> 00:03:12.900
All right !

00:03:13.820 --> 00:03:15.900
Aren't you glad we came ?

00:03:17.750 --> 00:03:20.770
I hope you have everything
you need to enjoy the resort.

00:03:20.770 --> 00:03:23.490
Yeah, we don't get
to come here that often.

00:03:23.490 --> 00:03:26.000
I've got to make the most
of my time at the ocean !

00:03:27.550 --> 00:03:28.500
What ?

00:03:28.500 --> 00:03:31.600
I feel worse about it
now that we're here.

00:03:31.600 --> 00:03:33.540
What're you
complaining about now ?

00:03:33.540 --> 00:03:35.560
I don't like the gig.

00:03:35.560 --> 00:03:38.700
I worked hard to
get this gig !

00:03:38.700 --> 00:03:42.360
Our music isn't for people
who just want to kill time.

00:03:43.120 --> 00:03:45.340
We can't be choosy
about the work we take !

00:03:45.340 --> 00:03:47.450
How can you be
so casual about this ?!

00:03:48.500 --> 00:03:51.360
Ray has to pay back the
rental company for damages.

00:03:51.360 --> 00:03:53.390
We're struggling
with that as it is !

00:03:53.390 --> 00:03:55.350
Who's the one who destroyed
that shuttle anyway ?!

00:03:55.350 --> 00:03:58.870
That's why I've been trying
to get higher paying gigs.

00:03:58.870 --> 00:04:01.550
Still, all I hear
are complaints !

00:04:04.260 --> 00:04:06.550
I have been waiting
for you, Miss Mylene.

00:04:21.040 --> 00:04:22.730
Would you
like a drink ?

00:04:22.730 --> 00:04:25.770
Hey, why are you here ?!

00:04:25.770 --> 00:04:28.150
Mayor Miria was concerned...

00:04:28.150 --> 00:04:31.820
...so I am now responsible for making
sure you get around safely.

00:04:32.390 --> 00:04:37.480
Oh, man. All she had to do was
give us the high paying gig.

00:04:37.480 --> 00:04:39.100
These are dangerous times.

00:04:39.860 --> 00:04:40.690
Listen !

00:04:40.690 --> 00:04:44.320
If you spy on me while pretending to be
guarding me, you won't get away with it !

00:04:44.320 --> 00:04:46.100
Yes.
I understand.

00:04:47.990 --> 00:04:50.560
This is 3-0-3. Nothing to
unusual to report in this region.

00:04:50.560 --> 00:04:52.920
Roger. Continue your patrol.

00:04:53.980 --> 00:04:55.400
The factory ship Three Star...

00:04:55.400 --> 00:04:59.060
...the food supply ship Iowa and the
scientific research ship Einstein...

00:04:59.060 --> 00:05:02.910
...have been assigned additional
VF-11 Thunderbolt escorts.

00:05:03.670 --> 00:05:06.140
Escorts have also been assigned
to the resort ship Riviera.

00:05:09.410 --> 00:05:15.550
My heart of love soars into tomorrow,
leaving a glowing red trail.

00:05:15.550 --> 00:05:20.500
Scatter the excitement and smile.

00:05:20.500 --> 00:05:28.150
A heart of love is inside everyone.
Sparkling flames of telepathy.

00:05:28.150 --> 00:05:36.100
Growing emotions are aerodynamic.
My charging heart of love.

00:05:38.940 --> 00:05:40.800
Let's go right on
to the next one !

00:05:40.800 --> 00:05:42.510
Wait, Basara !
That's not...

00:06:07.700 --> 00:06:13.750
Let's get started, it's Saturday night.
How're you guys doing ?

00:06:13.750 --> 00:06:17.870
Let's stand up,
do you feel the beat ?

00:06:20.000 --> 00:06:25.800
This is a flying paradise.
A forgotten energy...

00:06:25.800 --> 00:06:26.900
Now hurry up...

00:06:27.210 --> 00:06:28.620
You ruined it !

00:06:28.620 --> 00:06:30.100
What ?

00:06:30.100 --> 00:06:33.050
It's the audience's fault
if they weren't into it.

00:06:33.050 --> 00:06:34.170
You're wrong !

00:06:34.170 --> 00:06:37.120
I said we'd sing nice ballads
when I agreed to take this gig !

00:06:37.120 --> 00:06:38.750
Huh ?
What's that about ?

00:06:38.750 --> 00:06:40.440
What do you mean
"What's that about ?"

00:06:40.440 --> 00:06:43.050
You went right into
playing only fast songs !

00:06:43.050 --> 00:06:44.260
It's all right.

00:06:44.260 --> 00:06:45.600
It is not !

00:06:45.830 --> 00:06:48.500
Ray, you knew about this ?

00:06:49.600 --> 00:06:50.200
Yeah.

00:06:50.200 --> 00:06:52.170
You kept playing
all those fast songs.

00:06:52.170 --> 00:06:55.450
Shut up already.
I'll sing the songs I want.

00:06:55.770 --> 00:06:58.520
Fire Bomber isn't
just your band.

00:06:58.520 --> 00:06:59.700
Then whose is it ?

00:06:59.700 --> 00:07:01.460
It's all of us !

00:07:01.460 --> 00:07:03.630
It's your fault for
getting a gig like this.

00:07:03.630 --> 00:07:07.890
Geez. You selfish, irresponsible,
inconsiderate jerk !

00:07:07.890 --> 00:07:10.130
Why don't you think
of the band a little !

00:07:10.130 --> 00:07:12.840
Just let it go.
Let's go for a swim.

00:07:16.600 --> 00:07:23.260
Our voices synchronize just like
falling in love and kissing.

00:07:24.700 --> 00:07:31.700
My heart is always here for you.

00:07:33.200 --> 00:07:35.500
But, oh! I wonder...

00:07:58.260 --> 00:07:59.750
Aren't you going
to the ocean ?

00:07:59.750 --> 00:08:01.540
I'm taking a nap.

00:08:34.110 --> 00:08:36.320
Sorry for making you wait.

00:08:37.120 --> 00:08:41.400
Oh, have a seat.
Did you find this place okay ?

00:08:41.400 --> 00:08:43.770
Yes. Are your injuries
better already ?

00:08:44.950 --> 00:08:47.250
